; demo-events.aura — deterministic event stream used by the scenario.
;
; Returns a fixed list of events with a known distribution of user-ids,
; deltas (+/-), and timestamps so the engine's tier promotion, retraction,
; and checkpoint behavior can be exercised in a stable, repeatable way.
;
; Each event has shape (event user-id delta ts).
;
; Layout of the stream (17 events total):
;   * Mostly small positive deltas for two "regular" users (u1, u2).
;   * One "power" user (u3) that gets touched many times so promotion to
;     the sorted tier fires.
;   * A couple of negative deltas (retractions) to exercise retract-safe
;     semantics.
;   * A late event (timestamp < prior watermark) so the watermark path is
;     actually traversed.
;   * One "spammer" key (u9) whose bucket overflows past the overflow
;     tier cap so the eviction path is taken.
;
; Timestamps are strictly non-decreasing except for the deliberately-late
; event at the end.

(define (api demo-events-build)
  (list
    (list 'event 'u1 +1  10)
    (list 'event 'u1 +1  20)
    (list 'event 'u2 +2  30)
    (list 'event 'u1 +3  40)
    (list 'event 'u3 +1  50)
    (list 'event 'u2 -1  60)
    (list 'event 'u3 +1  70)
    (list 'event 'u1 +2  80)
    (list 'event 'u3 +1  90)
    (list 'event 'u3 +1 100)
    (list 'event 'u3 +1 110)
    (list 'event 'u2 +1 120)
    (list 'event 'u3 +1 130)
    (list 'event 'u3 +1 140)
    (list 'event 'u9 +1 150)
    (list 'event 'u9 +1 160)
    (list 'event 'u1 -2   5)))
